    "result_text": "All 30 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a runtime exception in the `rest.advice` package, mirroring the existing `CityAtCapacityException` pattern, carrying the rejected registration date.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT = 100` constant and a `rejectDailyLimitReached()` guard that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count reaches the limit. It's invoked in `addOwner` before persisting, alongside the other rejection checks.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DailyOwnerLimitException` returning `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) with a `ProblemDetail` body consistent with the existing handlers.\n\nThe provided `Cp19Tests` acceptance test (create 100 owners dated today, expect the 101st rejected with 429) passes, and the full suite (30 tests) is green. Seed owners have a NULL `registration_date`, so they don't count toward the daily total.",
